<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy" %>

<article class="prose prose-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white rounded-xl border border-surface-container shadow-sm p-8">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Last updated: <%= Date.new(2026, 5, 28).strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %></p>

  <p class="mb-6">
    Email Classifier ("we", "us", or "our") provides a service that automatically
    classifies and organizes email in your connected Gmail account based on rules you
    configure (the "Service"). This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect,
    how we use it, and the choices you have. By using the Service you agree to the
    practices described here.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address, used to create and authenticate your account via a magic-link sign-in.</li>
    <li><strong>Google account data.</strong> When you connect Gmail, we receive an OAuth access token that lets the Service read, label, and modify messages in your mailbox in order to apply the rules you create.</li>
    <li><strong>Rules and configuration.</strong> The classification rules, conditions, and actions you define.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage and log data.</strong> Technical information such as IP address, browser type, and timestamps, collected automatically to operate and secure the Service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">2. How We Use Information</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li>To provide, maintain, and improve the Service.</li>
    <li>To read and classify your email and apply labels or actions according to your rules.</li>
    <li>To authenticate you and secure your account.</li>
    <li>To communicate with you about the Service, including service-related notices.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations and enforce our terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">3. Google User Data</h2>
  <p class="mb-4">
    Email Classifier's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" class="text-sky-700 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">How we access Google data</h3>
  <p class="mb-4">
    When you connect Gmail, we request the <code>gmail.modify</code> OAuth scope, which allows us to
    read messages, apply and remove labels, mark messages as read, and move messages to trash — all
    on your behalf and only according to the rules you configure. We also request
    <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code>, and <code>profile</code> to authenticate your account.
    No access occurs outside of running your rules or re-authenticating your session.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">How we use Google data</h3>
  <p class="mb-4">
    Gmail data is used exclusively to execute the classification rules you define. We read message
    metadata (sender, subject, labels) and body content only to evaluate rule conditions and apply
    the corresponding actions. We do not use Gmail data for advertising, profiling, training machine
    learning models, or any purpose unrelated to the classification features you have requested.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">How we store Google data</h3>
  <p class="mb-4">
    OAuth access tokens and refresh tokens are stored encrypted in our database and are used solely
    to authenticate API requests on your behalf. Email content (message bodies, subjects, sender
    addresses) is fetched transiently at rule-processing time and is <strong>not persisted</strong>
    to our database. Application logs may temporarily contain metadata (e.g., message IDs, rule
    match results) for operational purposes; these are retained for a limited period and then
    deleted. You can disconnect Gmail at any time, which permanently removes your stored tokens.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">How we share Google data</h3>
  <p class="mb-4">
    We do not sell, rent, or share your Gmail data with third parties for their own purposes. Data
    may be processed by infrastructure service providers (hosting, database) acting on our behalf
    under confidentiality obligations. We do not allow humans to read your email content except
    where required for security incident investigation, to comply with applicable law, or with your
    explicit prior consent. We do not transfer Gmail data in connection with advertising, credit
    evaluation, or any data brokerage use.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">4. How We Share Information</h2>
  <p class="mb-3">We do not sell your personal information. We share information only:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li>With service providers (such as hosting and infrastructure vendors) who process data on our behalf under confidentiality obligations.</li>
    <li>When required by law, legal process, or to protect the rights, safety, and security of users or the public.</li>
    <li>In connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, subject to this Policy.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">5. Data Retention</h2>
  <p class="mb-6">
    We retain your account information and configuration for as long as your account is active.
    Email content is processed to apply your rules and is not stored beyond what is necessary to
    provide the Service. You may delete your account at any time, after which we delete or
    anonymize your data except where retention is required by law.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">6. Security</h2>
  <p class="mb-6">
    We use industry-standard technical and organizational measures to protect your information,
    including encryption in transit and restricted access to credentials. No method of
    transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">7. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li>You can disconnect Gmail at any time, which revokes our access to your mailbox. You may also revoke access from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" class="text-sky-700 hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions</a> page.</li>
    <li>Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or export your personal data. Contact us to exercise these rights.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">8. International Users</h2>
  <p class="mb-6">
    Your information may be processed in countries other than your own. Where required, we use
    appropriate safeguards for cross-border transfers.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">9. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p class="mb-6">
    The Service is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age in your jurisdiction),
    and we do not knowingly collect their personal information.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p class="mb-6">
    We may update this Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise
    the "Last updated" date. Material changes may be communicated through the Service.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">11. Contact Us</h2>
  <p class="mb-2">
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, contact us at:
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6"><a href="mailto:guillermo.siliceo@gmail.com" class="text-sky-700 hover:underline">guillermo.siliceo@gmail.com</a></p>
</article>
